# North star — {{RK_SLOT_PROJECT_NAME}}

This is the campaign's north star: the single result the repository exists to establish, or to
honestly refute. `rk init` seeded it so the id `.rk/config.json`'s `northStarId` names resolves to
a real node from day one — without it, `rk check`'s critical-path provenance check (every node on
the path to this result must carry cross-vendor, non-batch validation) would have an empty path to
walk and would report itself satisfied while covering nothing.

**Class: campaign-seed.** Stamped once, yours from here on. `rk upgrade` never rewrites this file,
and nothing regenerates it — edit it freely; it is not boilerplate. This header block is prose, not
a schema field: delete it once the shard has real content.

Edit checklist, in the order these usually come up:

- `contract:` is the one-line canonical statement and the join key for everything else. Once an
  `af` workspace exists it is byte-matched against that workspace's root conjecture, so a change
  here is a change there. Keep it one line.
- `kind:` is `theorem` as stamped. Change it to `open-problem`, `proposition`, or any other value
  in `argument/README.md`'s kind list if that is the honest shape of the target.
- `status:` starts at `conjecture`, the bottom of the rigour ladder. It moves up only when an
  external oracle certifies it (`CLAUDE.md` L0). Nothing promotes it automatically, and nothing
  should promote it by hand.
- `deps:` and `routes:` are absent, i.e. empty. Add the results this one rests on as they appear —
  `deps:` for unconditional prerequisites (AND), `routes:` for alternative sufficient sets (OR).
  Every id added here joins the critical path, which is the whole point of the file.
- `defs:` lists the `definitions/` ids the statement uses.
- `workspace:` and `af:` come later, when the proof is seeded in `af` (see `rk verify --help`).

Renaming this shard is a deliberate, logged act, and it is three edits, not one: rename the file,
change `id:` to the new filename stem, and change `.rk/config.json`'s `northStarId` to match. Do
only some of them and `rk check` FAILS with `configured north star ... could not be resolved` — the
check fails closed rather than degrading to a silent pass.

Full frontmatter contract: `argument/README.md`.
